Explanation:

The tangent plane to $Y_1$ at $(0,0,0)$ has normal vector $chevron.l 0, 0, 1 chevron.r$, giving $z=0$. The tangent plane to $Y_2$ at $(0,0,0)$ has normal vector $chevron.l 2, 0, 1 chevron.r$, giving $2x+z=0$. The tangent line to their intersection curve is the line of intersection of these two planes, which is the $y$-axis ($x=0, z=0$), parameterized by $bold(r)(t) = chevron.l 0, t, 0 chevron.r$.
